{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConsentDropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8Trackers17ConsentDropReportO","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/ConsentDropReport"},{"text":"> { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait until they are read. A record dropped for room is reported as it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dropped; while that report waits unread, later ones merge into it, one report counting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them all across their timestamps. So the reports waiting unread hold at most one overflow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"report between any two others (denials and finished trackers), however many events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overflow. The sequence has one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consumer, and ends once the consent is gone."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop of held or recovered records, in the order they happen.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers\/Consent"]]},"metadata":{"title":"dropReports","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"Trackers"}],"externalID":"s:8Trackers7ConsentV11dropReportsScSyAA0B10DropReportOGvp","fragments":